# SynapDome AT Linux mobile lab

The authorized operator's Android lab runs on this Linux server, not on a Mac.
Use /opt/synapdome-tools/bin/adb, serial emulator-5554, and ADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:127.0.0.1:5037.
Frida 17.8.2 is installed in /opt/synapdome-tools/frida. Use /opt/synapdome-tools/bin/frida-ps -H 127.0.0.1:27044 for process enumeration; frida-server runs inside Android through this loopback ADB forward.
The live screen is /mobile/vnc.html?autoconnect=true&resize=scale&path=mobile/websockify on the same HTTPS site, protected by the operator login.
First verify Android boot and tool connectivity before claiming tests ran. Request the authorized target APK/package and scope before app testing. A new device does not contain the operator's old app or sessions.
Do not wipe the emulator, stop unrelated processes, expose control ports, or change the authentication gateway during a test. Keep evidence in /var/lib/synapdome-ui/engagements. Do not print provider secrets or copy them into evidence.
When the operator takes manual control, stop automated taps/text input until they ask to resume. There is no automatic UI control-lock implemented yet.
DeepSeek is the configured provider. Do not attempt Windows/Ollama connections. Scanner API integration is separate; do not claim queued scanner runs occurred without a run ID and results.
